On the other hand, traditional machine learning approaches initially focused on a single level of structural information, such as local neighborhood patterns, global topological features, or quasi-global connectivity \cite{al2006link}. Subsequently, methods evolved to incorporate multiple topological similarities as features\cite{Chang2016,Yuan2021}, which is arguably the most intuitive approach. However, these methods still heavily rely on manually crafted heuristics. Consequently, they not only require significant human effort but also depend on domain-specific knowledge, thereby limiting their generalizability across different fields.

