\section{Results} \label{results}
In this study, five instruction-tuned LLMs were evaluated:
Llama‑3.2‑3B‑Instruct, a compact 3 billion‑parameter model;
Llama‑3.3‑70B‑Instruct, its 70 billion‑parameter counterpart \citep{grattafiori2024llama3herdmodels};
Qwen2.5‑Coder‑32B‑Instruct, a 32 billion‑parameter model specialized for coding;
Qwen2.5‑14B‑Instruct‑1M, a 14 billion‑parameter variant fine‑tuned with a context window of one million tokens; and QwQ‑32B, a general‑purpose 32 billion‑parameter model \citep{qwen2025qwen25technicalreport}. Models were evaluated on the 84 benchmark questions at a sampling temperature (T) of 1.0. To verify statistical stability, each model–prompt pair was sampled both 100 and 25 times; observed performance differences between these two sampling sizes were under 1\%. Consequently, 25 repetitions per prompt were deemed sufficient and used for all reported results. 

