\subsubsection{Inducing Language Preference Bias}
To evaluate the causal role of the identified ``CPP'' neuron, Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct was rerun on the benchmark with artificially amplified activation of the same neuron (L27 N6859). The resulting shift in language selection frequencies, demonstrating an increase in CPP output, is shown in Fig. \ref{fig:ll3b_cpp}.
\begin{figure}[!htb]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[width=1.0\linewidth]{ Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct_25_temp1_topPK_clamped_RERUN_3.png}
