\subsection{Additional Controlled Experiments}
To establish more definitive evidence for memorization effects, we propose two controlled experiments:

\paragraph{Synthetic Issue Generation} Create artificial but realistic GitHub issues for existing SWE-Bench repositories using LLMs, ensuring no training data overlap while controlling for repository familiarity and coding style consistency.

\paragraph{Repository Anonymization} Test models on SWE-Bench tasks where repository names, file paths, and other identifying information are systematically anonymized or replaced with synthetic equivalents, i.e. mutation on the repository snapshots. This avoids model using memorized information, and evaluate them solely on their problem solving abilities

