As a corollary of Theorem \ref{theo:33}, we obtain {\sf PSPACE}-completeness for intermediate positions of the Maker-Maker game on hypergraphs of rank 4. Note that, since we consider played moves that were not necessarily optimal, this does not imply any hardness result for \makermaker{$4$}.

\begin{corollary}
    Deciding whether the first player has a winning strategy for the Maker-Maker game on a hypergraph of rank 4 with one round (one move of each player) having already been played is {\sf PSPACE}-complete.
\end{corollary}

