\section{Conclusion}

In this paper, we explored the design space of diffusion-based \acrshort{nsc}s by investigating which conditioning/output configuration produces the best speech quality. The proposed designs were compared to \acrshort{sota} \acrshort{gan} and \acrshort{dm} baselines through objective and subjective evaluation. According to our findings, the best proposed design was \mTm{}, where a \acrshort{dm} generates enhanced mel-spectra from quantized mel-spectra. \mTm{} performed better than other \acrshort{dm}-based baselines proposed in the literature, but fails to improve on the results of \EC{}, a \acrshort{sota} \acrshort{gan}-based codec.

