It can be seen that the effect of the security rate threshold on the URPR and USRPR can be ignored. 
This is because increasing the secrecy rate threshold denotes higher security requirements, which leads to the requirement for more power.
Fig. \ref{fig05c} represents the minimum UPRP corresponding to the QoS threshold. 
With the increase of the QoS threshold, the URPR of Schemes 1 and 2 remains constant, while that of SDMA decreases in the high-requirement region. This is because SDMA needs more power for the same requirement.	

