\medskip 
The proof is analogous to the one for $(E \mapsfrom_{1} +)$.
\bigskip


\item The induction steps for $(\bot -)$, $(\top -)$, $(I \lor -)$, $(E_{1} \lor -)$, $(E_{2} \lor -)$, $(I_{1} \land -)$, $(I_{2} \land -)$, $(E \land -)$, $(I \mapsfrom -)$, $(E \mapsfrom -)$, $(I \to-)$, $(E \to_{1} -)$, $(E \to_{2} -)$ are symmetrical with the induction steps for $(\top +)$, $(\bot +)$, $(I \land +)$, $(E_{1} \land +)$, $(E_{2} \land +)$, $(I_{1} \lor +)$, $(I_{2} \lor +)$, $(E \lor +)$, $(I \to +)$, $(E \to +)$, $(I \mapsfrom +)$, $(E \mapsfrom_{1} +)$ and $(E \mapsfrom_{2} +)$, respectively, so their proofs are committed. The steps for $(\top-)$ and $(\land -)$ also use Lemmas \ref{lemma:exfalsotop} and \ref{lemma:conjunctionongeneral} instead of \ref{lemma:exfalsobot} and \ref{lemma:disjunctiongeneral}.

