\noindent Assume that $\Gamma;\Delta\Vdash^+\bot$. Then, by \ref{c:2int+}, $\Gamma;\Delta\Vdash_{\mathcal{B}}^+\bot$ holds for any base $\mathcal{B}$. Take $\mathcal{C}$ extending $\mathcal{B}$ such that $\Vdash_{\mathcal{C}}^+\gamma$ and $\Vdash_{\mathcal{C}}^-\delta$, for all $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and all $\delta\in\Delta
