\noindent The following key findings emerge from this analysis:\\

\noindent {\bf Key Finding 1: \emph{The diversity constraint serves a distinct purpose from fairness constraints in\cite{e17}.}} The Fair-NFR (black points) does not achieve the favorable cost-diversity trade-offs that our Diverse-NFR (blue points) achieves. This suggests that fairness metrics alone are insufficient for meeting diversity goals, and explicitly incorporating the entropy constraint is necessary.\\

\noindent {\bf Key Finding 2: \emph{Fairness and diversity constraints can coexist without sacrificing favorable trade-offs.}} Fig. \ref{fig3} shows that the favorable trade-off of Diverse-NFR (blue points) is maintained when applying fairness constraints—both strict (\( c_f = 0.1 \), red points) and less strict (\( c_f = 0.3 \), magenta points)—allowing for simultaneous fairness and diversity requirements to be effectively met.\\

