\begin{keypoints}
\item We present a fast, differentiable multiphase Lattice Boltzmann library in Python, built with JAX and scalable across CPUs, GPUs, and distributed systems.
\item The library models multiphase flows using the Shan-Chen method with support for arbitrary equations of state and includes modifications for independently tuning wettability and surface tension.
\item The library features decoupled compute and write precision, utilities for direct visualization of GPU arrays, and achieves giga-scale lattice updates per second on multi-GPU setups.
