  \label{fig: nodes_reaction_time}
\end{figure}

\subsubsection{Discussions}
In summary, our experiments validate the significant advantages of simultaneous sensor triggering combined with adaptive synchronization. Key advantages include:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Precision}: Simultaneous triggering substantially reduces synchronization errors.
    \item \textbf{Robustness}: Adaptive fusion windows effectively mitigate abnormal latencies and message drops.
    \item \textbf{Scalability}: Consistent and bounded reaction times show strong scalability in complex, real-world deployments.
\end{itemize}

Collectively, these results firmly establish the effectiveness and practical superiority of our delay-aware synchronization protocol over traditional synchronization methods, crucially enhancing reliability in real-time, multi-node infrastructure perception.

